 (scope . "Repaired v1.00.30 W4 guarded compiled-root activation (issue #9690): .github/actions/prepare-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/restore-racket-environment/action.yml, .github/actions/setup-racket/action.yml, .github/workflows/ci.yml, scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt, scripts/ci/prepared-env-report.rkt, ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root-workflow.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-ci-runtime-contract.rkt, tests/test-w9-ci-workflow-verification.rkt, artifacts/ci-recovery/v1.00.30-w4/** and artifacts/ci-topology/v1.00.26-w2/**, reviewed read-only against the frozen W4 wave doc in .planning/campaigns/96974d2cd97b152f99d296d6956f13b4f3b2bc4f79428894f74a1f3df49753d8/plan-snapshot/ and the BLOCKED-w4 repair list.")
 (report . "Round 4 review (independent, read-only VERIFY subagent) against implementation head ba35b090f78f00cc287133f2b77792fa836919cd (content digest ca5174f339b0ef53dbfc404aa9b16be88e8d7bca3feca1582b8a99b2b8d311e8) returned REQUEST_CHANGES with two substantive gaps: (1) with COMPILED_ROOT=off and a successful prepared-env restore no eager compile ran at all (the resolve step is skipped, the compile gate was skipped, and the fast suite lazily compiled after the purge), contradicting the documented off semantics and this wave's 'a miss compiles once eagerly' acceptance criterion; (2) the W4 telemetry the frozen wave doc requires was not emitted: the restore record hard-coded compiled-code-outcome eager-full-path (false on a root hit and after a restore), the root fields defaulted to unknown, the producer cost was never passed, and the launcher wrote no telemetry file while the map was uploaded before the shard ran. Both were fixed and committed at ba35b090f78f00cc287133f2b77792fa836919cd: the one bounded eager gate now also runs on the off lane and records its measured duration; the restore record classifies both the root axis (verified-root-hit|eager-fallback|global-off) and the code axis (mounted-verified-root|bounded-eager-gate|eager-full-path) from what the job actually ran, passes the producer job's measured cost and the gate's fallback cost, omits any unobserved cost, and the launcher writes its usable-root telemetry with the map uploaded after the shard. Stale comments were corrected and the compiled-root-mode input description now matches the code. New committed tests cover the telemetry wiring. The declared Verify chain is green at the head (182 focused tests, arch 32/32, security 64/64, workflows 33/33, check-deps OK, metrics --lint, provenance lint, fast 1208/1208) and retained at raw/verify-chain.txt. Round 5 is solicited against this head; this entry is updated with that verdict and its narrative before the implementation pull request is merged. History: round 3 returned REQUEST_CHANGES with four lane-wiring defects (hyphenated shell env var parsed as a shorter variable under set -u; the lane expression published Q_CI_COMPILED_ROOT=auto which both CLIs rejected; the fast-shard launch step never exported the lane switch so the launcher's flags file was ignored; the restore action materialized the verified root into the checkout), all fixed and reproduced. Round 1 returned REQUEST_CHANGES with three blocking findings (producer input never passed; zero-module run refused; merge commit instead of linear history) and round 2 with five (failed metrics lint in the retained capture; stale trio; wrong branch name; setup could touch a restored root without opt-in; zero-module run untested); all were fixed and are recorded in the campaign history and the red-first captures."))